    "rules": {"x": 4600, "y": 0, "w": 420, "size": "m", "fill": "blue", "text": "The five rules these screens follow\n\n1. Navigate by what you manage. Every object has one home.\n2. One way to edit: read-only by default, Edit opens the same drawer everywhere.\n3. One save model: Save applies it. Writing services.yaml and pushing to Traefik Manager happen after it; anything pending shows in the header only.\n4. Update in place: sections refresh live, never the whole page. Each says how old it is.\n5. Fast first paint: last known state at once, live data swaps in behind it.\n\nAll data is example data (the repository is public)."}
